  "methodology": "Skill coverage = sum(O*NET importance \u00d7 self-rated level) / sum(importance), using role skills rated at least 3 of 5. Levels: learning 0.25, working 0.65, strong 1.0. Score = min(100, coverage \u00d7 100 + 5 for a selected role interest). Requires 3 confirmed skills. Years and location do not alter the score. This is a heuristic, not a probability or forecast. Critical gaps have importance \u22654.",
  "limitations": [
    "Skill fit is the existing heuristic, not a forecast, hiring probability or local vacancy claim.",
    "US O*NET requirements describe occupations; your preferred location does not establish local demand.",
    "Showing up to 3 roles, 3 priority gaps per role and 6 reviewed SDG links. Other relationships may exist.",
    "Gap fractions reflect self-reported proficiency relative to a particular role. SDG relevance is not measured impact or endorsement.",
    "No AI agents, AI signals or forecasts are connected to this view."
  ]
